/*!
@defgroup trng
@ingroup mod_security True Random Number Generator (TRNG)
@brief Hardware entropy source module for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The TRNG module provides a hardware entropy source that samples an internal
ring oscillator, applies built-in statistical checks, and exposes the resulting
entropy words through the ENT register bank. The SDK driver offers a compact
polling workflow for initializing the peripheral, waiting for a validated
entropy block, and reading the generated data.

@section trng_features Key Features
- Generates entropy blocks through the ENT[] register bank.
- Supports device-dependent entropy block sizes of four or eight 32-bit words.
- Performs built-in long-run, monobit, and frequency-count monitoring.
- Supports configurable entropy delay, sample size, retry count, and
  statistical thresholds through the low-level configuration shadow.
- Supports optional system-clock forcing and divided TRNG clock output.
- Exposes status conditions for entropy-valid, frequency-count-valid,
  frequency-count-fail, and hardware-error handling.

@section trng_standards Supported Modes

The TRNG driver supports the following operating modes and usage styles:

| Mode / Usage Style         | Key Setting or API Path                  | Description                                                   |
|----------------------------|------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| Default polling mode       | TRNG_DRV_Init() + TRNG_DRV_GetStatus()   | Recommended flow for waiting until a validated block is ready.|
| Entropy readout            | TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent()                       | Copies the ENT register bank into a caller-supplied buffer.   |
| Low-level custom setup     | trngCfgSetting + TRNG_Set_*()            | Allows manual threshold, clock, and interrupt programming.    |
| Error/status servicing     | TRNG_GetStatusFlag(), TRNG_ClearStatusFlag() | Inspects and clears low-level status conditions.          |

@subsection trng_modes_entropy Device-Dependent Entropy Word Count
| Condition                                                     | ENT Words Read by TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent() |
|---------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE not defined or not equal 1 | 8 words                              |
| FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE == 1                      | 4 words                              |

@section trng_arch Module Architecture

The TRNG module is organized in a two-layer architecture:

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Application Code                │
│        (calls TRNG_DRV_* functions)          │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│        TRNG Driver Layer (trng_driver.h/c)   │
│  ● Instance-based polling API                │
│  ● Starts entropy generation and reads ENT[] │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│   TRNG HW Access Layer (trng_hw_access.h/c)  │
│  ● Direct register programming helpers       │
│  ● Status/entropy register accessors         │
│  ● Shared configuration shadow               │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│            TRNG Peripheral Hardware          │
│   (CTRL, STAT, SDCTL, FRQ*, SCM*, ENT[])     │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection trng_arch_driver Driver Layer (trng_driver.h)
Application code typically uses the TRNG driver layer only. The public driver
accepts a zero-based instance index, resets the TRNG, loads the internal
default configuration, applies the requested entropy delay, and starts a new
entropy-generation cycle.

@subsection trng_arch_hw HW Access Layer (trng_hw_access.h)
The hardware-access layer exposes the shared `trngCfgSetting` configuration
shadow together with helper functions for programming protected registers,
reading entropy words, and checking or clearing status conditions. Use this
layer only when the default polling driver is not sufficient.

@section trng_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection trng_config_struct trng_config_setting_t Fields
| Field                   | Type            | Description                                                | Default Value from TRNG_DRV_GetDefaultConfig() |
|-------------------------|-----------------|------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| lrunMax                 | uint32_t        | Long-run test threshold.                                   | 0x22                                           |
| retryCnt                | uint8_t         | Retry count before reporting an error.                     | 0x0F                                           |
| forceSystemClockEn      | bool            | Use the system clock instead of the ring oscillator.       | false                                          |
| clkOutputEn             | bool            | Output the divided TRNG clock for debug observation.       | false                                          |
| oscDiv                  | trng_osc_div_t  | Divider applied to the ring oscillator.                    | TRNG_OSC_NO_DEVIDER                            |
| frqCntInterruptEn       | bool            | Enable frequency-count-fail interrupt generation.          | false                                          |
| entroptValidInterruptEn | bool            | Enable entropy-valid interrupt generation.                 | false                                          |
| hwErrInterruptEn        | bool            | Enable hardware-error interrupt generation.                | false                                          |
| sampleSize              | uint32_t        | Number of entropy samples collected per generation cycle.  | 0x200                                          |
| entropyDelay            | uint32_t        | Delay inserted between entropy samples.                    | 0x1A0 (replaced by TRNG_DRV_Init() parameter)  |
| frqMin                  | uint32_t        | Minimum accepted frequency-count value.                    | 0x00000010                                     |
| frqMax                  | uint32_t        | Maximum accepted frequency-count value.                    | 0x003FFFFF                                     |
| monobitRange            | uint32_t        | Monobit range threshold.                                   | 0x2F0                                          |
| monobitMax              | uint32_t        | Monobit maximum threshold.                                 | 0x300                                          |
| pEntValue               | uint32_t *      | Optional pointer reserved for entropy-buffer management.   | NULL                                           |

@subsection trng_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                               | Description                                                          |
|-------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_INSTANCE_COUNT                 | Number of TRNG instances supported by the device.                    |
| TRNG_ENT_COUNT                      | Number of entropy words implemented in the device register bank.      |
| FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE | Selects the reduced entropy-read path used by TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent().    |
| TRNG_TRNG_INT_IRQS_CH_COUNT         | Number of interrupt channels exposed by the TRNG instance.           |

@section trng_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection trng_usage_basic Pattern 1: Initialize, Poll, and Read One Entropy Block
Initialize the TRNG with an entropy delay, wait until a validated block is
ready, and copy the entropy words into a software buffer.

@code{.c}
#define INST_TRNG (0U)

#if defined(FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE) && (FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE == 1U)
#define TRNG_WORD_COUNT (4U)
#else
#define TRNG_WORD_COUNT (8U)
#endif

uint32_t entropy[TRNG_WORD_COUNT] = {0U};
status_t status;

TRNG_DRV_Init(INST_TRNG, 0x0A00U);

do
{
    status = TRNG_DRV_GetStatus(INST_TRNG);
} while (status == STATUS_BUSY);

if (status == STATUS_SUCCESS)
{
    TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent(INST_TRNG, entropy);
}
@endcode

@subsection trng_usage_stream Pattern 2: Read Consecutive Entropy Blocks
Reading the highest ENT word clears the current block and starts the next
generation cycle. Poll again before reading the next block.

@code{.c}
#define INST_TRNG (0U)

#if defined(FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE) && (FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE == 1U)
#define TRNG_WORD_COUNT (4U)
#else
#define TRNG_WORD_COUNT (8U)
#endif

uint32_t firstBlock[TRNG_WORD_COUNT] = {0U};
uint32_t secondBlock[TRNG_WORD_COUNT] = {0U};

TRNG_DRV_Init(INST_TRNG, 0x0800U);

while (TRNG_DRV_GetStatus(INST_TRNG) == STATUS_BUSY)
{
}
if (TRNG_DRV_GetStatus(INST_TRNG) == STATUS_SUCCESS)
{
    TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent(INST_TRNG, firstBlock);
}

while (TRNG_DRV_GetStatus(INST_TRNG) == STATUS_BUSY)
{
}
if (TRNG_DRV_GetStatus(INST_TRNG) == STATUS_SUCCESS)
{
    TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent(INST_TRNG, secondBlock);
}
@endcode

@subsection trng_usage_lowlevel Pattern 3: Inspect Low-Level Status and Test Results
The low-level helper APIs can be used to inspect validation counters and clear
status conditions after an error or test failure.

@code{.c}
#define INST_TRNG (0U)

TRNG_Type *const trngBaseTable[TRNG_INSTANCE_COUNT] = TRNG_BASE_PTRS;
TRNG_Type *base = trngBaseTable[INST_TRNG];
uint32_t frequencyCount;
uint32_t monobitCount;

if (TRNG_GetStatusFlag(base, TRNG_FREQUENCY_COUNT_FAIL))
{
    frequencyCount = TRNG_Get_FRQCNT(base);
    monobitCount = TRNG_Get_SCMC(base);
    TRNG_ClearStatusFlag(base, TRNG_ALL_STATUS);
}
@endcode

@section trng_api API Quick Reference

@subsection trng_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function              | Description                                                  |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_DRV_Init()       | Reset the TRNG, load default configuration, and enable it.   |
| TRNG_DRV_DeInit()     | Restore the TRNG register block to its default state.        |

@subsection trng_api_entropy Entropy Data Access
| Function              | Description                                                  |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent()    | Copy the current entropy block from the ENT register bank.   |

@subsection trng_api_status Status Query
| Function              | Description                                                  |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_DRV_GetStatus()  | Report whether entropy generation is busy, ready, or failed. |

@subsection trng_api_hwctrl Module Control
| Function              | Description                                                  |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_Enable()         | Enable the TRNG module.                                      |
| TRNG_HW_Init()        | Restore the TRNG registers to their reset values.            |
| TRNG_Disable()        | Disable the TRNG module.                                     |
| TRNG_SWReset()        | Request a software reset through the CTRL register.          |

@subsection trng_api_hwcfg Configuration Register Programming
| Function              | Description                                                  |
|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_Set_CTRL()       | Program CTRL from the shared configuration shadow.           |
| TRNG_Set_SDCTL()      | Program SDCTL from the shared configuration shadow.          |
| TRNG_Set_FRQMIN()     | Program the minimum frequency-count threshold.               |
| TRNG_Set_FRQMAX()     | Program the maximum frequency-count threshold.               |
| TRNG_Set_SCML()       | Program the monobit thresholds.                              |

@subsection trng_api_hwdata Data & Status Access
| Function                 | Description                                               |
|--------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| TRNG_Get_FRQCNT()        | Read the frequency-count result after validation.         |
| TRNG_Get_SCMC()          | Read the monobit counter value.                           |
| TRNG_Get_ENT()           | Read one entropy word from the ENT register bank.         |
| TRNG_GetStatusFlag()     | Read one low-level TRNG status condition.                 |
| TRNG_ClearStatusFlag()   | Clear one status condition or all writable status bits.   |

@section trng_notes Important Notes

@subsection trng_notes_clock Clock Dependency
The TRNG peripheral clock must be enabled before calling TRNG_DRV_Init() or
any low-level TRNG helper. Use @ref clock_manager to configure and enable the
device clock tree.

@subsection trng_notes_delay Entropy Delay Range
TRNG_DRV_Init() only applies the requested entropy delay when
`entroyDelay <= 0xFFFFU`. Larger values are ignored silently because the API
returns no status. Passing an out-of-range value leaves the hardware
unmodified.

@subsection trng_notes_read Entropy Read Side Effect
Reading the highest valid ENT register clears the current entropy block and
starts the next generation cycle. Mixing partial low-level ENT reads with
TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent() can cause the caller to lose part of a block.

@subsection trng_notes_device Device Variations
Devices that define `FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE == 1` use the reduced
entropy-read path in TRNG_DRV_Get_Ent(), which updates only the first four
destination words. Size entropy buffers according to the device variant, or
use `TRNG_ENT_COUNT` / `FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE` to select the
buffer length at compile time.

@subsection trng_notes_defaults Driver Configuration Scope
The public driver API exposes only the entropy-delay parameter. All other TRNG
thresholds, retry counts, clock-selection fields, and interrupt enables come
from the internal defaults loaded by TRNG_DRV_GetDefaultConfig(). Use the
hardware-access layer if custom low-level configuration is required.

@section trng_integration Integration Guide

@subsection trng_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source files must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/trng/trng_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/trng/trng_hw_access.c
@endverbatim

@subsection trng_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directories to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/trng/
@endverbatim

@subsection trng_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required for this module. Device feature
macros such as `FEATURE_TRNG_ENTROPY_COUNT_OPTIMIZE` and `TRNG_ENT_COUNT` are
provided by the selected device header.

@subsection trng_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager - Required for TRNG clock enable and clock-tree setup.

*/
